WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.868
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:08.970
NATALIE VAIS: Let's say
you want to build an app.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.430
Not just any app, but
a serverless, scalable,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.380
mobile-thinking,
analytical IoT app.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.990
If you do a quick
Google search, you

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.110
will get 1.2 billion
results on how to do this.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.590
So where do you start?

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.830
My name is Natalie Vais,
and I'm a Product Manager

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.390
on Cloud Firestore.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.690
Today, I want to talk to you
about building amazing apps,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.940
specifically, how
to build globally

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.103
scalable apps with
Cloud Firestore.

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:34.020
If you're starting a new
project from scratch,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.520
and you want to
build it yourself,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.080
you'll likely have to think
about a couple of things--

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.340
number one, setting up
a database, number two,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.730
creating some kind of API layer
on top of it so you can make

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.410
queries from your clients.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.560
And that probably means, third,
creating an authentication

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.230
service to make sure
users can only access

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.640
data they're supposed to.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.710
And then lastly,
making sure your data

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.690
syncs with your
local results which

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.600
are probably being stored in
a completely separate client

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.960
database.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.099
Now, just make sure it works
across multiple platforms.

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:08.190
It can easily handle things
like spotty network connections.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.630
Simple, right?

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.460
As soon as your app goes viral--

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.923
fingers crossed for you--

00:01:12.923 --> 00:01:14.340
all of a sudden,
you have to worry

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.890
about scaling, high
availability, and disaster

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.360
recovery strategies.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.900
And you'll probably need to hire
more people to manage it, too.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.690
Or you can just use
Cloud Firestore.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.240
Cloud Firestore is
a fully managed,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.690
serverless, NoSQL document
database purpose-built

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.470
for solving some of the toughest
problems of mobile web and IoT

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.240
app development today.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.590
In many ways, it's
more than a database.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.280
It's an entire back
end for your apps.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.800
To create Firestore,
we learned from two

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:46.140
other popular
databases at Google--

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.680
Firebase Realtime Database
and Cloud Datastore--

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.320
usage patterns have shifted
since those architectures

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.630
were designed some 7 to 10
years ago, respectively.

00:01:55.630 --> 00:01:57.700
So we took a close look
at the developer wish

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.390
list for each of these
to inform the products.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.430
You can think of
Firestore as the best

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.260
of both of these worlds.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.294
Cloud Firestore
handles all the things

00:02:06.294 --> 00:02:08.669
that you don't want to think
about when you're developing

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:13.470
a mobile app, so you can really
focus on your core business.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.770
The first thing to know is
that Cloud Firestore is fully

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.290
supported in the Firebase SDKs.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.140
This includes web,
iOS, and Android,

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.440
so you can access data
directly from these clients.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.980
This works in conjunction with
Firebase Auth and Security

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:29.640
Rules.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.800
And those things
allow you to control

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.090
who has access to read and
modify data on the server.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:38.950
There's that Auth layer we
mentioned at the beginning.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.790
You wouldn't believe how
normal it has become for people

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.920
to look at their apps
when there is absolutely

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.130
no chance of connectivity.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.010
A person checks their phone an
average of 80 times in a day,

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.380
so it's becoming increasingly
common for people

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.340
to expect our apps to work
offline and across devices.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.070
With Cloud Firestore,
the client libraries

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.370
already come with full
support for offline mode.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.340
The SDK handles conflict
resolution on-device

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.130
and syncs up with the
server when you reconnect.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:12.040
Because we built Cloud Firestore
with a serverless architecture,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.640
you don't have to worry
about provisioning, capacity

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.860
planning, scaling,
or maintenance.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.650
There are servers
distributed across the world,

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:22.440
just not ones that
you have to manage.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.720
All of this is taken
care of by the system.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.620
Scaling is automatic and
happens as an online operation.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.500
Say goodbye to
maintenance windows.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.590
On top of that, Cloud Firestore
is built for the Cloud.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:38.220
That means it's replicated
across zones and regions

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:41.010
depending on how you
choose to configure it.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.250
In this year alone, and as part
of going generally available,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.310
we added 10 new locations
to Cloud Firestore.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:50.100
Replication across
data centers is really

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.830
one of those things you want
to outsource if you can.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.570
It becomes complicated
quickly and has

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.120
a huge overhead for ops teams.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.730
With this replication,
you get five nines

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.130
SLA for multi-region
and a four nines

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.270
SLA for regional deployments.

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.740
This is one of the highest
availability services we offer.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.620
All of this lets you focus
on your core business

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.680
and leaves the infrastructure
to Google Cloud,

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.480
which is our core business.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.670
With over 1 million
databases created already,

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:21.480
Cloud Firestore has
seen a huge diversity

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.540
of workloads already deployed
within our customer base.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:28.050
The unifying themes among
these workloads include--

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.150
number one, the
need for data access

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.970
even when connectivity
lapses; number two,

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:36.030
scalability for many
users across platforms;

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.280
and number three, the
ability to move quickly

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.390
from prototype to production.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:44.160
And that's Cloud Firestore--
your auto-syncing, auto-scaling

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.600
database in the Cloud.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.390
Give it a try, and find out why
it's the most discussed cloud

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:49.650
database on Stack Overflow.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:53.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

